        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">A follow on from <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3719174104\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42351\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42351/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42351\">#42351</a> this adds the <code class=\"notranslate\">Sec-CH-Width</code> in same way. I missed it originally as couldn't see it supported as missed the key point that it's only sent on images requests (add this to the docs toot to save the next person!)</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fix developer confusion: <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/ericportis.com/post/3m7oa4vo5fk2q\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bsky.app/profile/ericportis.com/post/3m7oa4vo5fk2q</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://www.tunetheweb.com/experiments/sec-ch-width/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.tunetheweb.com/experiments/sec-ch-width/</a></p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/527851131-983a9338-9902-47e8-b3e5-607fbe9190cb.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..GmynDs8nP8c3ZtrYRd5kHtssUQSxImT10nfN0oooW6A\"><img width=\"2000\" height=\"1558\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/10931297/527851131-983a9338-9902-47e8-b3e5-607fbe9190cb.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..GmynDs8nP8c3ZtrYRd5kHtssUQSxImT10nfN0oooW6A\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 1558px;\"></a>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">BCD data: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3740976900\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28690\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28690/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28690\">mdn/browser-compat-data#28690</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42453",
            "title": "Add Sec-CH-Width",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-19T07:52:41.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-18T00:38:12.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tunetheweb",
                "url": "https://github.com/tunetheweb"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60345799?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Changes a <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;select&gt;</code> value in a playground to be read after each change of the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;select&gt;</code>, correctly reacting to the change.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Display/Multi-keyword_syntax#display_block_flow-root_and_display_inline_flow-root\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">display: flow-root</code> playground</a> has a <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;select&gt;</code> toggle, which is supposed to change the <code class=\"notranslate\">display</code> value of some elements to demonstrate the effects of the <code class=\"notranslate\">flow-root</code> value.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Currently, its value is read only once when the playground JS is first executed, which results in <code class=\"notranslate\">display: block</code> always getting set on the elements.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42437",
            "title": "Fix `display` toggle in playground not changing value",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-18T11:40:20.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-17T10:52:40.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Kiwow",
                "url": "https://github.com/Kiwow"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">While using the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Storage_Access_API\" rel=\"nofollow\">Storage Access API</a>, when embedded content activates a previously-granted <code class=\"notranslate\">storage-access</code> permission via the <code class=\"notranslate\">requestStorageAccess()</code> method or the <code class=\"notranslate\">Activate-Storage-Access</code> header, 3rd party cookies are now only sent with requests to the calling embed's exact origin.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Previously, 3rd party cookies were sent with requests to the calling embed's site.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This behavioral change has occurred in:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Chrome 141: See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5169937372676096\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5169937372676096</a>.</li>\n<li>Firefox 140: See <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/storage-access-api/requestStorageAccess-cross-origin-fetch.sub.https.window.html?run_id=5176618970775552\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/storage-access-api/requestStorageAccess-cross-origin-fetch.sub.https.window.html?run_id=5176618970775552</a></li>\n<li>Safari is the only browser left that still supports the old model.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds content to document this change.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/cfredric/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/cfredric\">@cfredric</a> / <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/hamishwillee/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/hamishwillee\">@hamishwillee</a>.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42432",
            "title": "Technical review: storage-access activation per origin not site",
            "date_modified": "2025-12-19T18:09:24.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-12-16T18:24:16.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130252722?u=e2ea277a897162968e6f29c2b4f5e9889e4fee39&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Added a note about the required Node.js version.</p>\n\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Just a Quick Heads Up in the README file for what node version the project requires exactly</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Even though it’s just a small edit, this prevents setup errors like the one I encountered (EBADENGINE) when using Node.js &lt; 24. This heads-up ensures contributors know the minimum Node.js version required to build the site.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #42415.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3732535243\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42415\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/42415/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42415\">#42415</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
